2014 WL 2216367, at *1 (N.D. Cal. May 29, 2014) (\"Federal Rule of Civil Procedure 55(b)(2) provides for a court ordered default judgment after an entry of default under Federal Rule of Civil Procedure 55(a).\" (citing Penpower Tech. Ltd. v. SPC Tech., 627 F. Supp. 2d 1083, 1088 (N.D. Cal. 2008))). Plaintiffs' 51 motion for entry of default (corrected) is DENIED. This was an apparent attempt to circumvent their procedural error of failing to seek entry of default first, by merely renaming the filing. Compare ECF No. 51, with ECF No. 50. The Clerk of Court is instructed not to enter default in this matter. The Court admonishes Plaintiffs' counsel for failing to abide by the Federal Rules of Civil Procedure and the Court's Civil Standing Order in filing these motions. As to the latter, Plaintiffs' counsel noticed a hearing on the motions for 2/11/2026, without reserving a hearing date with the Courtroom Deputy, in contravention of Section V of the Civil Standing Order. (This is a text-only entry generated by the court. There is no document associated with this entry.) (ekllc1, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 2/10/2026) (Entered: 02/10/2026)", "tags": []}]}